/E (This visualization clearly shows that Logistic Regression provides the best overall performance, mainly due to its strong classification of positive and negative reviews, while performance on neutral reviews remains weak across all models.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
900 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Overall, the results provide several important findings. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
901 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (First, the analysis confirms that extreme sentiments \(positive and negative\) are easier to classify compared to neutral reviews. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
902 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Second, the class imbalance in the dataset affects model performance, especially for the neutral class. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
903 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Third, simpler models such as Logistic Regression can outperform more complex models when working with TF-IDF features. )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
904 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Finally, the findings highlight the importance of improving feature representation and balancing the dataset in future work to enhance model performance.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
